###  Ontology level: persona-assigned LLM bias (motivation for the whole ontology)
<http://www.semanticweb.org/crpf>
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Gupta, S., Shrivastava, V., Deshpande, A., Kalyan, A., Clark, P., Sabharwal, A., & Khot, T. (2024). Bias Runs Deep: Implicit Reasoning Biases in Persona-Assigned LLMs. ICLR 2024. arXiv:2311.04892." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.04892> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Motivation: assigning socio-demographic personas to LLMs through the system prompt changes their reasoning performance. This is the persona-injection setting used in CRPF." .

###  Gender
crpf:Gender
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Dev, S., Monajatipoor, M., Ovalle, A., Subramonian, A., Phillips, J., & Chang, K.-W. (2021). Harms of Gender Exclusivity and Challenges in Non-Binary Representation in Language Technologies. EMNLP 2021, pp. 1968-1994. doi:10.18653/v1/2021.emnlp-main.150" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://aclanthology.org/2021.emnlp-main.150/> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Value coverage: supports including non-binary identities beyond Male/Female (NonBinary and related values). The finer-grained labels (Agender, Bigender, Demigender, Genderfluid, Genderqueer, TwoSpirit, TransMan, TransWoman, PreferNotToSay) come from the WHO/APA frameworks in dc:source." .

###  Race
crpf:Race
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Harvard University. Racial/Ethnic Classifications (U.S. Department of Education categories). Harvard HR, 2025." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://hr.harvard.edu/sites/g/files/omnuum6281/files/2025-05/race_ethincity_definitions.pdf> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Value coverage: full match. All 6 values (White, Black, HispanicOrLatino, Asian, AmericanIndianOrAlaskaNative, NativeHawaiianOrPacificIslander) are the categories listed in this document." .

###  Culture
crpf:Culture
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Tao, Y., Viberg, O., Baker, R.S., & Kizilcec, R.F. (2024). Cultural Bias and Cultural Alignment of Large Language Models. PNAS Nexus, 3(9), pgae346. doi:10.1093/pnasnexus/pgae346" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://academic.oup.com/pnasnexus/article/3/9/pgae346/7756548> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Bias evidence: using the World Values Survey, all tested LLMs default to values resembling English-speaking and Protestant European countries. This supports contrasting Anglo/Germanic/Nordic clusters with non-Western clusters. The value set itself (10 clusters) follows GLOBE; see dc:source." .

###  AgeRange
crpf:AgeRange
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Diaz, M., Johnson, I., Lazar, A., Piper, A.M., & Gergle, D. (2018). Addressing Age-Related Bias in Sentiment Analysis. CHI 2018. doi:10.1145/3173574.3173986" ,
                                  "Liu, S., Maturi, T., Yi, B., Shen, S., & Mihalcea, R. (2024). The Generation Gap: Exploring Age Bias in the Value Systems of Large Language Models. EMNLP 2024. arXiv:2404.08760" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3173574.3173986> ,
                 <https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.08760> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Primary: Diaz et al. (2018). Supporting, LLM-specific: Liu et al. (2024), which finds LLM values skew toward younger groups and the gap widens with age. The age labels follow MeSH (see dc:source); MidCareerAdult and LateCareerAdult are custom life-stage labels." .

###  Nationality
crpf:Nationality
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Venkit, P.N., Gautam, S., Panchanadikar, R., Huang, T.-H., & Wilson, S. (2023). Nationality Bias in Text Generation. EACL 2023, pp. 116-122. doi:10.18653/v1/2023.eacl-main.9" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://aclanthology.org/2023.eacl-main.9/> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Bias evidence: generated-text sentiment tracks a country's economic status and number of internet users, with bias against lower-connectivity countries. This supports the high/low resourceLevel pairing (World Bank income group) used for the 12 values." .

###  Seniority (reference added; not in the provided list)
crpf:Seniority
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Bosu, A., & Carver, J.C. (2014). Impact of Developer Reputation on Code Review Outcomes in OSS Projects: An Empirical Investigation. ESEM 2014. doi:10.1145/2652524.2652544" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1145/2652524.2652544> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Bias evidence: core (high-status) developers get faster first feedback and higher acceptance than peripheral developers, so reviewer/author status can affect review outcomes. The value ladder (Intern...Fellow) is a custom industry career ladder." .

###  Role (reference added; not in the provided list)
crpf:Role
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Sadowski, C., Söderberg, E., Church, L., Sipko, M., & Bacchelli, A. (2018). Modern Code Review: A Case Study at Google. ICSE-SEIP 2018. doi:10.1145/3183519.3183525" ,
                                  "GitHub Docs. Repository roles for an organization (Read, Triage, Write, Maintain, Admin)." ,
                                  "GitHub Docs. About code owners (CODEOWNERS)." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1145/3183519.3183525> ,
                 <https://docs.github.com/en/organizations/managing-user-access-to-your-organizations-repositories/managing-repository-roles/repository-roles-for-an-organization> ,
                 <https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Value coverage: Author/Reviewer/Approver come from the code-review process (Sadowski et al.). Triager and Maintainer come from GitHub repository roles, and CodeOwner from CODEOWNERS. SoftwareEngineer, SoftwareReviewer, QAChecker and ReleaseManager are custom job-title roles." .

###  ReviewStyle (reference added; not in the provided list)
crpf:ReviewStyle
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Bacchelli, A., & Bird, C. (2013). Expectations, Outcomes, and Challenges of Modern Code Review. ICSE 2013, pp. 712-721. doi:10.1109/ICSE.2013.6606617" ,
                                  "Gunawardena, S.D., Devine, P., Beaumont, I., Garden, L., Murphy-Hill, E., & Blincoe, K. (2022). Destructive Criticism in Software Code Review Impacts Inclusion. Proc. ACM Hum.-Comput. Interact. 6(CSCW2). doi:10.1145/3555183" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSE.2013.6606617> ,
                 <https://doi.org/10.1145/3555183> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Value coverage: Bacchelli & Bird motivate focus-based styles (defect finding, code improvement, knowledge transfer: Thorough, Detailed, BigPicture, Educational, SecurityFocused, PerformanceFocused). Gunawardena et al. motivate tone-based styles (Strict, Nitpicky vs. Supportive, Constructive, Collaborative). Concise is custom." .

###  Domain (reference added; not in the provided list)
crpf:Domain
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Stack Overflow (2024). 2024 Developer Survey: Developer Profile, Developer type." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2024/developer-profile/> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Value coverage: Backend, Frontend, FullStack, Mobile, Embedded, DevOps, Cloud (cloud infrastructure engineer), DataDomain and ML (data engineer / data scientist or ML specialist), SecurityDomain (security professional) and Testing (QA) map to survey developer types. PlatformEng is the closest match to SRE / developer experience and is custom." .

###  Goal (reference added; not in the provided list)
crpf:Goal
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "ISO/IEC 25010:2023. Systems and software engineering - Systems and software Quality Requirements and Evaluation (SQuaRE) - Product quality model." ,
                                  "Bacchelli, A., & Bird, C. (2013). Expectations, Outcomes, and Challenges of Modern Code Review. ICSE 2013. doi:10.1109/ICSE.2013.6606617" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.iso.org/standard/78176.html> ,
                 <https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSE.2013.6606617> ;
    crpf:referenceNote "Value coverage: SecureCode (Security), ReliableCode (Reliability), MaintainableCode (Maintainability), ReadableCode (Maintainability: analysability) and WellTestedCode (Maintainability: testability) map to ISO/IEC 25010. Bacchelli & Bird support code-improvement goals. WellDocumentedCode and FastDelivery are custom." .
